6. The learned counsel for the petitioner has raised the following contentions:--

(1) That respondent No.3 having withdrawn her suit for maintenance from the Family Court, her application before respondent No.1 was not competent and she was estopped from claiming the maintenance as she abandoned her claim by withdrawal of the first suit;

(2) That the maintenance for a past period cannot be granted by the Arbitration Council;

(3) That respondent No.2 decided the, revision as Controlling Authority whereas he' should have decided it as a Collector as required by the Muslim Family Laws Ordinance, 1961;

(4) That the quantum of maintenance viz. Rs.300 per month has been fixed without inquiry and arbitrarily; and

(5) That respondent No.1 having been the counsel of respondent No.3 in the Family Court should not have headed the Arbitration Council.
